{
  "summary": "This pull request introduces an optional `sat_vb` boolean parameter to the `getmempoolinfo`, `getnetworkinfo`, `estimatesmartfee`, and `estimaterawfee` RPCs. When set to true, fee rate fields are returned in sat/vB rather than BTC/kvB. It adds a `ValueFromFeeRate` helper in `core_io` that formats fee rates with fixed 3-decimal precision using integer division to avoid floating-point rounding errors on sub-1 sat/vB values.",
  "problem": "Bitcoin Core fee rates are expressed in BTC/kvB across RPC endpoints, whereas users and wallet ecosystems standardly operate in sat/vB. Consumers must perform client-side conversions that risk rounding inaccuracies (especially below 1 sat/vB) and create unnecessary friction for API integrations.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Returning feerates in BTC/kvB it can be very burdensome and is not good practice, as the most widely adopted units are sat/vB. This PR aims to show a PoC of how we could migrate to sat/vb in a backwards compatible manner.'",
    "PR description: 'Because of sub 1sat/vB environment we cannot rely on GetFee() because it internally uses FeeFrac EvaluateFee() function which rounds the values to always return an int. If the feerate < 1 then it will be rounded to 1 or 0.'"
  ],
