    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "For `estimatesmartfee`, adding `sat_vb` as the third parameter shifts the `options` argument from index 2 to index 3 for positional RPC callers, which also affected several functional test invocations.",
  "changed_since_previous": "The implementation approach remains the same as the previous version; positional argument handling and functional tests were adjusted to accommodate the added parameter index.",
  "card": "This pull request adds an optional sat_vb boolean parameter to getmempoolinfo, getnetworkinfo, estimatesmartfee, and estimaterawfee, enabling callers to receive fee rates formatted in sat/vB instead of BTC/kvB. It addresses friction and calculation bugs caused by modern wallet software having to convert legacy BTC/kvB rates client-side, especially when handling sub-1 sat/vB rates. Values are formatted via a new fixed-point helper without floating-point conversion. The PR serves as a proof of concept for issue #32093 and has no external dependencies.",
